__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Broad on purpose -- *.db/*.db-wal/*.db-shm alone missed real backup snapshots named
# atlas.db.pre-<ticket>-bak, atlas.db-shm.pre-<ticket>-bak, etc. (DEVH-114, real incident:
# several GB of production warehouse content got committed locally before push, caught before
# it reached GitHub). *.db* catches every variant of that shape, not just the exact names.
*.db*
.DS_Store
# Runtime state, not source -- these are live operational artifacts (queued registry writes,
# quarantined ingest rows), not code, and can carry real production content.
**/staging/pending-assertions.jsonl
**/quarantine/*.jsonl
venv
ROADMAP.md
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.json.pre-*
ARCHITECTURE-REVIEW.md
prepare_notebook.py
repo_context_part_*.txt
# token_bloat_diagnostic's OUTPUT, never its source. This is the public repo, and meta.projects_seen
# in that report enumerates every project directory on the machine -- 35 of them, including several
# that have nothing to do with this repo and should not be inferable from it. The tool is worth
# publishing; a machine-wide directory census is not. Root cause is the tool's own --project-hint
# being broad enough ("m5-dev-") to match everything, which also left meta.scope_warning null, so
# the report gave no sign it had over-collected. Narrow the hint when regenerating; do not commit
# the output either way.
token_bloat_diagnostic.json
token_bloat_diagnostic.txt
# Unreviewed binary. Nothing goes into a public repo that has not been read, and a PDF cannot be
# read by the scan that cleared the files around it.
dev-harness Run 2 build.pdf
# Credential-target descriptors are machine-local configuration: each one names a specific tool
# installed on a specific machine, and the filename alone discloses which. The committed part is
# example.sh.template, which is not matched by this pattern. Write your own descriptor from it.
bollard/lib/credential_targets/*.sh

# Session-continuity artifacts (handoff docs) are internal operational notes for the next
# working session, not something the public needs -- this repo ships the product, not a
# history of how it was built session to session.
HANDOFF-*.md
